@anon.c8777b812d6b35c09a8e6156f259107b.401 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [659 x i8] }> <{ [659 x i8] c"The Python interpreter into which packages should be installed.\0A\0ABy default, uv installs into the virtual environment in the current working directory or\0Aany parent directory. The `--python` option allows you to specify a different interpreter,\0Awhich is intended for use in continuous integration (CI) environments or other automated\0Aworkflows.\0A\0ASupported formats:\0A- `3.10` looks for an installed Python 3.10 in the registry on Windows (see\0A  `py --list-paths`), or `python3.10` on Linux and macOS.\0A- `python3.10` or `python.exe` looks for a binary with the given name in `PATH`.\0A- `/home/ferris/.local/bin/python3.10` uses the exact Python at the given path." }>, align 1
